@cellframenet: built to protect funds from quantum threats.

Layer 2 · Upgraded and live

@Algorand: Falcon-1024 accounts, 2.7M+ post-quantum transactions.
@PeraAlgoWallet: rekey an existing account to post-quantum.
@LuteWallet: Falcon accounts with password protection.
@NEARProtocol: ML-DSA signing on mainnet.
@blueshift: Winterwallet, Winternitz vaults on Solana mainnet.

Layer 3 · Testnet

@tezos: Quantumnet, staking with post-quantum keys.
@QANplatform: XLINK pairs EVM wallets with post-quantum keys.
@Starknet: a phone signed an ML-DSA transaction, verified onchain.
@SuiNetwork: ML-DSA-65 signatures in testnet releases.

Layer 4 · Proposals and research

@Aptos: AIP-137, opt-in SLH-DSA signatures.
@ethereum: EF post-quantum team targets L1 resistance by 2029.
@hedera: A post-quantum user key type targeted for 2027.
Bitcoin BIP-360: P2MR outputs drop the exposed key path.
@projecteleven: Strongpoint post-quantum custody.

Signatures move first, and consensus follows.

Chains that let holders rekey in one transaction will carry their users through the quantum migration.

